WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
You email a hotel.

2
00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.240
Perfect grammar. Perfect spelling.

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.080
And it opens with «Salut !» Then you email

4
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.820
a friend and sign off «Cordialement».

5
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.010
Something feels off.

6
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:16.330
The task allows anywhere
from 70 to 150 words.

7
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.870
So is longer always better?

8
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:23.370
So how can a 120-word
email be a perfect answer,

9
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.500
and why does one friendly
word sink an email to a hotel?

10
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.880
In this mission, you'll
turn a dial that runs

11
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.890
from friend to official.

12
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.900
Then you'll see the skeletons
of seven text types,

13
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.730
from blog to leaflet.

14
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: find out what makes
a short email a perfect one.
